        "locked": false,
        "title": "[Bug] Incomplete cleanup of expired pairing authorizations leads to memory growth in node registry",
        "body": "### Description\nWhen pairing new nodes, authorization session tokens are tracked in node-registry.ts. If the pairing flow is abandoned or times out, the registration callbacks are not properly cleaned up from event-mapper.ts event emitters. This creates dangling references that prevent the session objects from being garbage-collected.\n\n### Affected Files\n- src/acp/pairing/node-registry.ts\n- src/acp/pairing/event-mapper.ts\n\n### Proposed Solution\n1. Attach pairing event listeners with a single-use hook wrapper or explicitly dispose of them inside a timeout cleanup hook in node-registry.ts.\n2. Add test assertions in event-mapper.ts verifying listener counts return to baseline after pairing sessions expire.",
